        "text": "Page: Gül Mosque. Sentence: Gül Mosque (Turkish: \"Gül Camii\" , meaning: \"The Mosque of the Rose\" in English) is a former Eastern Orthodox church in Istanbul, Turkey, converted into a mosque by the Ottomans.\nPage: Hippodrome of Constantinople. Sentence: Today it is a square named \"Sultanahmet Meydanı\" (\"Sultan Ahmet Square\") in the Turkish city of Istanbul, with a few fragments of the original structure surviving.",
